Package: tornadoexposure
Type: Package
Title: Explore and Map ZCTA-Level Tornado Exposures in the United States
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Hailey", "Hansen", role = "aut"),
    person("Jessy", "Nguyen", role = "aut"),
    person("Prachi", "Sanghavi", role = "aut"),
    person("Kate", "Burrows", email = "kburrows@uchicago.edu", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Institute for Climate and Sustainable Growth (ISCG)", role = "fnd"),
    person("Center for Climate, Health and Society (CHAS)", role = "fnd"))
Description: This package contains data and functions to allow users to explore
    and map ZCTA-level tornado exposures in the United States from 1996 to 2025.
    Data comes from the NOAA Severe Weather Database and the Census Bureau.
    Tornadoes of magnitude EF 1 and greater are included in the dataset.
